ks stand quietly, providing a tranquil conclusion.\n\n**Key Points**\n\n- **Zebras** are the only mammals tracked across multiple frames (running early, then the same two individuals grazing/socializing).  \n- **Antelopes** appear in a single frame, solely running.  \n- **Birds** transition from a flock in flight to individual water‑bird behavior (ibis) and finally to stationary storks.  \n- **No lions** are visible in any frame.  \n\nThe sequence moves from high‑energy herd movement to increasingly subdued, individual moments, ending with stillness.', 'failed_images': []}}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '{\n    "tool": "RECORD",\n    "entries": [\n        "Time: 3131 seconds, Event: Male Lion lies on the ground, gazing directly at the camera (from character log)",\n        "Time: 3132 seconds, Event: Lioness with piercing yellow eyes gazing directly at camera (close-up)",\n        "Time: 3134 seconds, Event: Lion with piercing yellow eyes and dark pupils staring intensely at camera",\n        "Time: 3135 seconds, Event: Lion with tawny mane gazing intensely forward in close-up shot",\n        "Time: 3137 seconds, Event: Lion with piercing yellow eyes gazing intently at camera, whiskers and fur texture detailed",\n        "Time: 3138 seconds, Event: Majestic lion with piercing yellow eyes gazing intensely directly at camera",\n        "Time: 3139 seconds, Event: Lion with tawny mane and piercing yellow eyes gazing intently forward",\n        "Time: 3140 seconds, Event: Majestic lion gazing intently into camera in serene savannah landscape",\n        "Time: 3141 seconds, Event: Lion\'s face in close-up with intense golden eyes and light-brown mane",\n        "Time: 3142 seconds, Event: Majestic lion with golden mane and piercing yellow eyes gazing directly into camera",\n        "Time: 3143 seconds, Event: Majestic lion with golden-brown coat staring intensely into camera",\n        "Time: 3144 seconds, Event: Lion with piercing yellow eyes staring intensely forwa